# .gitignore for eql-interactive-map
#
# Deliberately minimal: only patterns this repo can actually produce. The build needs nothing
# but the Python 3 standard library, and npm is used solely by the verification harness under
# tools/verify/js. If a tool is ever added (a venv, pytest, coverage, a linter), add its
# pattern then rather than carrying boilerplate for tooling that isn't here.

# --- Python bytecode (scripts/build.py and the tools/verify Python layer) ---
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]

# --- Generated build output; rebuild with scripts/build.py, never commit ---
# Anchored to the repo root so it cannot swallow an unrelated nested dist/.
/dist/
# The author build exposes the repo-export/authoring surface and must never be committed.
# /dist/ covers its default output path; this also catches an --out build written elsewhere
# in the repo, and keeps holding if /dist/ is ever partly un-ignored to publish a prebuilt
# user map. Distribute the user edition instead.
*.author.html

# --- Regenerated map geometry (scripts/import_pack.py) ---
# The traced geometry is derived from a community map pack this project does not own, so it
# is converted from a user-supplied pack path rather than committed. Anchored to the repo
# root: the name is generic enough that an unanchored pattern could swallow something else.
/data/_generated/

# --- Verification harness: node deps and generated artifacts (tools/verify/run.py) ---
# _out/ collects screenshots and downloads, _fx/ the built fixtures. npm currently lives only
# in tools/verify/js, but node_modules/ is unanchored so a second npm location is covered too:
# nobody hand-authors that name, so matching at any depth costs nothing.
node_modules/
tools/verify/js/package-lock.json
tools/verify/_out/
tools/verify/_fx/

# --- Personal / machine-specific, never committed ---
# Both patterns match at any depth: the first covers layout.local.json and
# .claude/settings.local.json, the second a bare suffix such as config.local.
*.local.*
*.local
# Personal planning: specs, implementation plans, session handoffs, reference snapshots.
# Public-facing documentation goes directly in docs/ instead.
docs/internal/
